From 6707738ce5e134477a0f9480f53e5225d5cb08f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan <dev.in@gnu6.live>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(device-map): size Qwen3 MoE layers without expert stacks
 under residency

Under expert residency the expert stacks load host-side, but the GGUF device
mapper counted them in every layer, so only 15-16 of 48 layers fitted on an
8 GiB card and the count depended on free VRAM at load time. Mapped layers now
exclude the stacks and the cache budget is reserved once in the non-mapped size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016D4Xz7aLLGu873oZNF6vk4
